{#
  templates/policy-slug.hcl.j2 — the per-project `policy-<slug>` ACL.

  Rendered by tasks/main.yml (openbao_project_onboard) and written to
  sys/policies/acl/policy-{{ project_slug }} with a platform-admin-scoped token
  (NOT the Root_Token — the Root_Token is revoked after bootstrap; this role is
  a day-2 action). Mirrors the style of the sibling
  templates/platform-admin.hcl.j2 in openbao_init_unseal.

  This is the SINGLE enforcement point for the path-prefix + policy per-project
  isolation model (design.md: "Path-prefix + policy per-project isolation";
  Object shapes table row "Project policy"). OpenBao Community has no namespace
  primitive, so a project is isolated by (a) the `secret/<...>/<slug>/*` path
  convention and (b) THIS policy granting capabilities ONLY on that project's
  five KV v2 sub-paths — and NOTHING outside them (Req 1.2, 1.3).

  The five KV v2 sub-paths a token needs to fully CRUD+list a project's KV tree
  (Req 1.2) — KV v2 splits an operation across distinct API prefixes:
    secret/data/<slug>/*      — read/write the current secret VALUE
    secret/metadata/<slug>/*  — list keys + read/delete all-version metadata
    secret/delete/<slug>/*    — soft-delete specific versions
    secret/undelete/<slug>/*  — restore soft-deleted versions
    secret/destroy/<slug>/*   — permanently destroy versions
  No sixth path, no wildcard above the slug, no capability on any other
  project's prefix (Req 1.3 — a policy-<slug> token must be denied everywhere
  outside these five prefixes, returning no other project's data or metadata).

  NO secret value is templated here — this is an ACL document only. `project_slug`
  is read READ-ONLY from projects.yaml (this role never writes the registry).
#}
# MANAGED BY ANSIBLE (openbao_project_onboard) — DO NOT EDIT BY HAND.
# policy-{{ project_slug }}: per-project KV isolation (Req 1.2, 1.3).
# Grants create/read/update/delete/list on EXACTLY the five KV v2 sub-paths for
# this slug, and NO capability on any path outside them.
{% for sub in openbao_project_kv_subpaths %}
path "{{ openbao_kv_mount }}/{{ sub }}/{{ project_slug }}/*" {
  capabilities = [{{ openbao_project_policy_capabilities | map('to_json') | join(', ') }}]
}
{% endfor %}
